WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.440
The second season of The Umbrella Academy
may have answered some of our biggest lingering

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.820
questions from season one, but it raised a
bunch more of its own.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.700
Here are some of the biggest questions we're
still wondering about after finishing The

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.520
Umbrella Academy season two.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.560
In the first season of The Umbrella Academy,
we meet the Hargreeves siblings' "mom," Grace,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.800
whom we quickly learn is actually a robot.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.830
However, in season two, Diego runs into Grace
again at a gala in 1963 -- only this time,

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.800
she's a real, flesh and blood person.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.400
It turns out that Grace is a scientist dating
Reginald Hargreeves, the enigmatic Hargreeves

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.880
family patriarch, and has no knowledge of
any of his shadier dealings.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.700
Diego urges Grace to look closer at her boyfriend's
business in Dallas, telling her that Reginald

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.690
is planning to assassinate the president.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.660
Although Grace insists that Diego is mistaken,
she does take his advice, and finds evidence

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.440
of the assassination conspiracy.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.700
She confronts Hargreeves, who doesn't refute
any of her suspicions, but tells her there

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.320
are some parts of his life he just can't discuss
with her.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.900
"Someday, I hope to share it all with you.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.500
Until then, I'm asking you to trust me."

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.120
This doesn't seem to go over well with Grace.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.840
The last we see of her, she's walking away
from Reginald, seemingly for good.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.160
It raises a lot of questions, including how
the robot version of Grace eventually came

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.400
into being in the original timeline, and whether
Diego's interference has changed Grace's fate.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:29.039
Season one of The Umbrella Academy revealed
that 43 babies were spontaneously conceived

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.540
and birthed on October 1, 1989, and that Hargreeves
only managed to adopt seven.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.940
That leaves 36 still out there, somewhere.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.710
With the introduction of Lila, we get our
first glimpse of what might have befallen

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.180
some of those other children.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.980
Like the Hargreeves siblings, Lila has superpowers,
but her childhood was markedly different from

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:47.620
theirs.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:52.039
It begs the question of how many other superpowered
"siblings" are out there, if any of them have

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.380
found one another, and why we haven't heard
anything about them yet.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.800
Right on the heels of learning that she is
actually a long-lost Hargreeves "sibling,"

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.140
Lila grabs a briefcase and splits for destinations
unknown.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:07.100
Although Luther could have stopped her, Diego
intervenes, admitting that he's fallen in

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:07.980
love with her.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.160
But where did Lila go?

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:13.020
With a Commission briefcase, she could travel
to literally any point in history.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.880
And without a functional Commission to monitor
her, she could probably get away with quite

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:17.540
a lot.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:22.060
Will she go to 1993, to attempt to save her
parents from the Handler and Number Five?

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.600
Will she jump further into the future, to
try to reunite with Diego?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.220
One of the more poignant storylines from season
one revolved around the eccentric Klaus accidentally

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.920
spending several years fighting in the Vietnam
War.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.260
During that time, he fell in love with a fellow
soldier named Dave, who was tragically killed

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.060
in action.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.980
In season two, though, Klaus sees another
chance to save Dave when he finds himself

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.680
back in the '60s, this time several years
before his first trip back.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:51.120
Unfortunately, Klaus' plan isn't very well
thought out, and he winds up getting punched

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.520
in the face for his troubles.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.360
Yet despite Klaus' bumbling, he does actually
manage to change something.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.580
"I've already enlisted."

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.480
"What?

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.120
That's not supposed to happen yet."

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.120
Klaus assumes this means he's doomed, but
maybe not.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.380
Perhaps Dave's earlier enlistment date will
lead to other, bigger changes down the line.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.980
Could Klaus actually have managed to save
Dave after all?

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.980
We don't know, but we're holding out hope.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:19.840
When young Harlan accidentally drowns midway
through season two, Vanya uses her newly rediscovered

00:03:19.859 --> 00:03:22.680
powers to lift the water out of the lake and
revive him.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.829
During the process, she inadvertently passes
some of her powers to him, although she doesn't

00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:28.100
realize it at the time.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.320
Later, Vanya realizes Harlan is linked to
her, and that her own trauma has triggered

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.120
his powers.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.980
Harlan's powers quickly spiral out of control,
but Vanya is ultimately able to calm Harlan

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.360
enough to approach him and draw his powers
back into herself -- or so she thinks.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.280
At the end of the season, Harlan's mother,
Sissy, makes the hard choice to say goodbye

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.769
to Vanya, since she worries that Vanya's abilities
will put a target on her back that would put

00:03:50.769 --> 00:03:51.940
Harlan in danger.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:56.340
Sissy just wants a normal, safe life for her
son, and decides to take him to California

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.380
to start over.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.460
However, the last time we see Harlan, he's
making a toy bird levitate in his hand in

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:05.640
the back seat of his mother's car, implying
that Vanya didn't drain all of his powers

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.340
after all.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.219
What other abilities does Harlan still have,
and how will those powers and his traumatic

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.040
experience in Dallas help shape the rest of
his life?

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.160
We hope we'll find out in season three.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.880
One of the odder parts of the 1960s storyline
is the cult Klaus starts, thanks to his tendency

00:04:20.889 --> 00:04:24.801
to spout song lyrics that haven't been written
yet as if they're prophecies, and his ability

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:28.140
to use his dead brother to perform seemingly
impossible feats.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:33.240
Egged on by Klaus' own ego and aversion to
conflict, Klaus' cult quickly winds up taking

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:37.420
on a life of its own, and by 1963, he's amassed
quite the following.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.160
Although Klaus does eventually attempt to
make things right, revealing to his followers

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:45.730
that he's a fraud before leaving with his
siblings to save the world and return to 2019,

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:49.240
the cult members mistake his confession for
another pearl of enlightenment.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.780
Despite Klaus' departure, the closing moments
of season two indicate that his cult is far

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:54.780
from over.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.220
They're still driving around in a rainbow-hued
bus, picking up new acolytes along the way.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:03.580
It'll be interesting to see if the cult is
still around in 2019, how it has changed over

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:08.210
the intervening 56 years, and, perhaps most
intriguingly, how the group will react to

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.250
the return of their Prophet, still looking
exactly the same as he did when he disappeared

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.660
in 1963.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.380
When the Hargreeves siblings arrive back in
2019, they're shocked and relieved to find

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.060
both their father and their previously deceased
brother Ben are still alive.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:26.080
But their excitement is short-lived when neither
Reginald Hargreeves nor Ben seems to have

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.120
any idea who they are, nor what the Umbrella
Academy is.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.700
"This is the Umbrella Academy."

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:31.580
"Wrong again.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.860
This is the Sparrow Academy."

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.380
The name change is mystifying, since the Umbrella
Academy was named for the umbrella factory

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:43.400
where Hargreeves set up shop shortly after
arriving on Earth.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:48.300
He was still operating out of this same umbrella
factory in the 1963 that the Hargreeves siblings

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:53.540
departed before jumping to 2019, so it's curious
that the academy doesn't bear its name.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:57.220
Could someone else have named the Sparrow
Academy, and if so, what is their role in

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.280
the organization?

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.640
Is Hargreeves still in charge, or is he now
reporting to someone else?

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.800
And what significance does the name "Sparrow"
hold?

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:08.000
We can't help but think about how Harlan ended
the season using his powers to levitate a

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.700
toy bird.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.700
Coincidence?

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.600
We'll see.

